From 490e2b4a01f4b2d3edc9e075943d59cfd3b848b2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 20:48:47 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] fix(doctor): fourth review round - values that are argv,
 switches, quoting, speed

Leaks closed:
- a spaced env value (JAVA_TOOL_OPTIONS='-Xmx1g -Dapi.token=x',
  GIT_SSH_COMMAND='sshpass -p x ssh', CURL_ARGS='-u a:b') is judged as its
  own argv; shell text whose program word is a flag is passed as flags
- a flag inside a value (--jvm-arg=-Dpassword=x, JAVA_OPTS=-Dtoken=x)
- lists are split before a value is taken for a path
- URL queries are judged pair by pair (an e-mail stays one value), and a
  fragment after a masked path piece is masked as its tail
- mixed-case dotted key groups; -u/--user user:pass for any program
  (a bare user or a numeric uid:gid stays)

Over-masks fixed: secret-named switches no longer eat the next argument
(stdin suffix; ask/prompt/keep prefixes; main's kebab-case --flag rule and
its test restored); openssl -key/-keyout/-kdf (attached matching only for
flags listed as attached), -newkey/-keyform, key and cert file names after
a secret flag; digest-pinned images keep their name; model names via a
small model vocabulary; Go pseudo-versions; -Xlog:gc*, %r@%h:%p, globs.

Shell text is shown as written (quotes kept) unless masking changed a
word. The base64-neighbour pass is linear (25k pieces: 0.3 s, was minutes).
Dead branches removed (-D special case, path symbol rule); path/URL
handling split into named helpers.

Tests: positions for spaced env values, flag values and lists, a
mixed-case dotted key shape; ceilings and docstring state the same bounds
(10/5/3/2% tested, ~8/3/2/1% measured worst); the doctor test no longer
depends on the runner's random temp dir name.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
